# othello: the board takes a click as the player's move and the computer answers, choosing at random among its equal best moves after
# randomize(), so the script plays only control-clicks, which move and freeze the computer: a black move that flips one piece, a white
# answer that flips one, H shows the hints for the side to move, E evaluates the moves, U undoes the last move, Q quits.
move 600 500
wait
keydown Control_L
click 1 360 280
keyup Control_L
wait
keydown Control_L
click 1 360 360
keyup Control_L
wait
key H
wait
key E
wait
key U
wait
key Q
